{"run_id": "2026-11-01T23-24-smoke-execution-01", "unit": "execution", "item_id": "exe-0014", "model_id": "otel-llm-1.7b-it@2a2d417b", "adapter_id": "none", "grader": "rule-based-parser-v1", "test_set_sha256": "e0152332fba3d220e0e23af6068f127ef4c8cf12333d93efa9a3263c40007a63", "prompt_sha256": "9a359346b74df0ae6af74d9802f5cdae581250a558f18de0f41a265b6365ae87", "output": "The mean time a packet spends in the system is given by the formula $1/\\lambda$, where $\\lambda$ is the service rate. Substituting the given values, we get $1/323.0$ seconds. Converting this to milliseconds, we multiply by 1000, resulting in $3.103$ milliseconds. Final answer: 3.103", "output_sha256": "f407f1792a8c459a53a14bc8cef43bc4f774aedbdc7938ae4ea5e3ad88d47ab7", "output_tokens": 84, "truncated": false, "batch_started_at": "2026-11-01T23:28:56.213+00:00", "batch_finished_at": "2026-11-01T23:29:03.584+00:00", "batch_wall_s": 7.3709, "latency_s": 0.4607, "parsed": 3.103, "gold": 4.5106, "correct": false, "correct_loose": false}
{"run_id": "2026-11-01T23-24-smoke-execution-01", "unit": "execution", "item_id": "exe-0015", "model_id": "otel-llm-1.7b-it@2a2d417b", "adapter_id": "none", "grader": "rule-based-parser-v1", "test_set_sha256": "e0152332fba3d220e0e23af6068f127ef4c8cf12333d93efa9a3263c40007a63", "prompt_sha256": "8976e2b5d75d672047e947218c80c174612d15c33256b05b26db4ca4cf2a1bd7", "output": "The mean number of customers in the system for an M/M/1 queue is given by the formula $1/(1-\\rho)$, where $\\rho$ is the utilization. Substituting the given value of $\\rho = 0.543$, we get $1/(1-0.543) = 1/0.457 ≈ 2.187$. Final answer: 2.187", "output_sha256": "600ccb7c9044081c2721f0425115ff98d1d4ef420a2daa6902dee4996d1c01d7", "output_tokens": 94, "truncated": false, "batch_started_at": "2026-11-01T23:28:56.213+00:00", "batch_finished_at": "2026-11-01T23:29:03.584+00:00", "batch_wall_s": 7.3709, "latency_s": 0.4607, "parsed": 2.187, "gold": 1.18818, "correct": false, "correct_loose": false}
